   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the exact value of \\( \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\left(2 x + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = 2 x + 1 \\) and \\( dv = \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\), so \\( du = 2 \\, dx \\) and \\( v = - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            [
               "Cos",
               "x"
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[- \\left(2 x + 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral is \\( \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} - 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx = -2 \\).",
         "mathjson": -2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( 1 - \\left(-2\\right) = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      }
   ],
